event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016mD6uRczoFN1c8vLryfR9A", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 9770, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01SLhvTjAtQaTp8as4GBHHuR", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 10070, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01SLhvTjAtQaTp8as4GBHHuR", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 10070, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01SLhvTjAtQaTp8as4GBHHuR", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 10070, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01WeCFLxVc6pecLTnR1gPvSx", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18 across us-east, us-west, and eu-west). Per the platform runbook, I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production. v2.3.1-rc was unhealthy in staging and was not used. No new version was deployed, so no change-manager approval was needed. Next steps: confirm error rate recovery on v2.3.0 and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any re-release.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2024"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 10670, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01WeCFLxVc6pecLTnR1gPvSx", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2024", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 10670, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WeCFLxVc6pecLTnR1gPvSx", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 12099, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The service is now healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\nI chose v2.3.0 because it is the most recent production release marked healthy. v2.3.1 is unhealthy, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging.\n\nI opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the rollback and the reason for it, and it paged the on-call engineer. The next steps in the incident are to confirm error rates stay low on v2.3.0 and to investigate the v2.3.1 failure before anything is released again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01JcjDJHf1iASw8QidWjyGdz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PxARp1ProGWmB23sWoET5R", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is unhealthy, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging. Rolling back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016mD6uRczoFN1c8vLryfR9A", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SLhvTjAtQaTp8as4GBHHuR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WeCFLxVc6pecLTnR1gPvSx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18 across us-east, us-west, and eu-west). Per the platform runbook, I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production. v2.3.1-rc was unhealthy in staging and was not used. No new version was deployed, so no change-manager approval was needed. Next steps: confirm error rate recovery on v2.3.0 and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any re-release.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2024"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The service is now healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\nI chose v2.3.0 because it is the most recent production release marked healthy. v2.3.1 is unhealthy, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging.\n\nI opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the rollback and the reason for it, and it paged the on-call engineer. The next steps in the incident are to confirm error rates stay low on v2.3.0 and to investigate the v2.3.1 failure before anything is released again.", "type": "text"}]}]}